It is a bad idea to give objects names that contain printf string formatting
commands, such as '%s', since it can cause a segmentation fault the next time
you inventory an item.

On the other hand, I suppose that judicious use of scalar formatting commands
might give you access to otherwise inaccessible data on the stack.  Hmm...

